[32m[2025-07-27 18:09:13,506] [    INFO][0m - ['\n<s>\n\n    <|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\nDescribe how a Docker container works.<|eot_id|>\n\n    <|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\nA'][0m
[32m[2025-07-27 18:09:13,506] [    INFO][0m - [' Docker container is an isolated environment in which applications can be packaged and run. It consists of the application, system libraries, and other configuration files necessary for a specific task. The container runs within a docker host, which isolates the container from other host resources and is responsible for managing its life cycle. Docker containers are lightweight and highly portable; they can be quickly spun up and transported to different environments such as cloud, bare metal, and on-premises. Containers are isolated from the underlying host system so they can be securely run and managed. Docker also uses images which function like snapshots – making it easy to deploy and run applications reliably and consistently across different environments.<|eot_id|>\n\n'][0m
